    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is [by design](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/085baefa6aca44526be621b15e7b688f996c2daf/doc/mini.txt#L727-L733). It is usually helpful if cursor is inside some big covering region but you want to select next. If you don't like it, you can set search method to `'cover'` and use \"last\"/\"next\" mappings to select previous/next textobject.\r\n\r\nTruth be told, I a little bit regret this design decision after implementing \"last\"/\"next\" mappings, but originally they were not there. Also as you are not the first one to report this, I wonder how to make the note about this behavior more stand out.\r\n\r\nDuplicate of #116.",
